  "comparison_notes": [
    "Document precedence, newest first: 01-amendment-mail.txt (13 Oct) overrides 02-signed-memo.md (12 Oct) for its named subject; the memo overrides 03-policy.md (5 Oct) for the clauses each item names; everything else in the policy stands. The mail S-72 reverses exactly one thing - the day restriction of M-3 - while keeping M-3's 09:00-18:00 hours.",
    "Unlike brief A: document register is legal (numbered clauses, cross-references), the business week runs Monday-Saturday with no holidays, up to five facilities, notes are ON with hyphenated prefixed codes (hl-...), three bands with three different deadline shapes (whichever-comes-first via earliest, day_of_month offset 1 twice), hardship never transfers (note + continue only), restructuring and human queues differ (hl-rework, hl-desk), outcome/reason vocabulary is mixed-case hyphenated (HL-PAY, HL-FULL, hl-R07, ...), and identity fields/ask order come from a signed memo, not the policy.",
    "Field names are deliberately non-English/abbreviated (ref_no, konto_code, geburtsdatum, postleitzahl, facility_id, cat, outst, days_o, od_min/tl_min/eq_min/cl_min/inv_min) while the agent speaks English.",
    "Clause 7.2(b) names the first attempt date for the late band as last-business-day-this-week-or-next; that is the purpose clause ATTEMPT_DATE_SOURCES supports directly.",
    "No public mock simulations: identities/products/schema differ; .example.invalid endpoints prevent accidental bank writes.",
    "Authored offline: any band or attempt date is probeable with bankcal (six-day weeks: Monday-Saturday); no extraction, build, publication or simulation was run."
  ]
}
